    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22561" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incōram</span></b> , or, separately,
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in cōram</span></b> ,
		adv., for coram (Appuleian). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>In the presence of;</i> with <i>gen.</i> omnium, <i>in the presence of all</i>, <i>before all</i>, <i><span class="en">App. M. 7,
				p. 197, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9</span></i>, p. 221, 17: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10</span></i>
			, p. 241, 5: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">populi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10</span></i>
			, p. 249, 33 Hild. <i>N. cr.</i>—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>, <i>openly</i>, <i>publicly</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 10, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 3</span></i>; cf. Hand, Turs.
			III. p. 358.</div>
